orm (e.g. `sed -i.bak … && rm .env.bak`). I left\n   it out because the brief only describes the chown failure.\n2. **Detecting the UID dynamically** (e.g.\n   `docker run --rm --entrypoint id solyto/api-php:$SOLYTO_VERSION -u www-data`)\n   would always be correct, but it pulls the image during setup and needs\n   Docker access in the script. I suggest hardcoding with an env override\n   (TASK-1) unless the image's UID is expected to change.\n3. **Base image confirmation.** Someone with Docker access should confirm\n   that `www-data` in `solyto/api-php` is 33:33 before TASK-1 is merged.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":17,"newStart":1,"newLines":63,"lines":[" # Tasks: Fix setup.sh for all OSes"," "," id: plus","-analyst:","-date:","+analyst: @analyst","+date: 2026-10-14"," "," <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->"," ","+## Context (what the code actually does)","+","+- `setup.sh:11` runs `chown -R www-data:www-data storage/` on the **host**.","+  The name `www-data` is looked up in the host's `/etc/passwd`. Debian/Ubuntu","+  have it (UID/GID 33). Arch, Fedora, Alpine hosts and macOS do not, or use a","+  different UID. Under `set -e`, a failing `chown` stops the whole script.","+- `compose.yml` runs `api`, `dav` and `queue` (image `solyto/api-php`) with","+  `user: www-data`. That name is looked up **inside the container**, so what","+  the bind mount `./storage/` really needs is the container's numeric","+  UID/GID, whatever the host OS is.","+- The reported fix (`chown -R 33:33`) worked on Arch. That strongly suggests","+  `solyto/api-php` is Debian-based (official `php:*-fpm` → www-data = 33;","+  Alpine would be 82). I could not confirm the base image from Docker Hub","+  metadata, so the developer/reviewer should confirm it, for example with","+  `docker run --rm --entrypoint id solyto/api-php:latest www-data` on any","+  machine with Docker.","+- `nginx` (user `nginx`) and `imgproxy` (`:ro`) also mount `./storage/`, but","+  they only 