 unclear scope (not turned into tasks)","+","+1. **Other non-portable parts of setup.sh.** \"All OSes\" may mean more than","+   the chown. `sed -i -e …` (setup.sh:20-25) is GNU-only. On macOS/BSD,","+   `-i` takes the next argument as a backup suffix, so it will misbehave or","+   leave a `.env-e` file. If macOS hosts are in scope, a follow-up task could","+   swap it for a portable form (e.g. `sed -i.bak … && rm .env.bak`). I left","+   it out because the brief only describes the chown failure.","+2. **Detecting the UID dynamically** (e.g.","+   `docker run --rm --entrypoint id solyto/api-php:$SOLYTO_VERSION -u www-data`)","+   would always be correct, but it pulls the image during setup and needs","+   Docker access in the script. I suggest hardcoding with an env override","+   (TASK-1) unless the image's UID is expected to change.","+3. **Base image confirmation.** Someone with Docker access should confirm","+   that `www-data` in `solyto/api-php` is 33:33 before TASK-1 is merged."]}],"originalFile":"# Tasks: Fix setup.sh for all OSes\n\nid: plus\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UQiEKkYdrMDSVHbEiCJ8Cg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
